# Cretli — previewing a page

To open, look at, screenshot or debug a web page (a running app or the Cretli UI
itself) use the built-in Browser through the Cretli MCP tools `browser_*`. The user
sees the same tab in the **Browser** panel.

1. `browser_open { url }` → `browserSessionId` + `browserTabId` (it adopts the
   session the user already opened in the panel).
2. `browser_screenshot` (returns a file path), `browser_dom`, `browser_console`,
   `browser_network`; in Agent mode also `browser_navigate` and `browser_input`.

Rules:

- Do **not** launch your own Playwright/Chromium for a preview, and do not probe
  for a debug port or another browser profile.
- If the page shows a sign-in, ask the user to sign in in the Browser panel of
  this chat. Never look for credentials, cookies or session tokens in `.env` or
  `data/`.
- When a `browser_*` call fails, report the error code; it says what the user has
  to do (open the chat in the UI, free the session, allow the origin).

Automated end-to-end tests still use the project's Playwright configs. Full guide:
the `cretli-browser` skill (`.agents/skills/cretli-browser/SKILL.md`).
